  data:  # 32f7
    kind: work_item  # 32f7
    title: "go: a method on a package function's result (slog.New(h).Error, json.NewEncoder(w).Encode) keeps the package slot and is credited to the same-named package function (INV-vusum residual)"  # 32f7
    status: todo_hard  # 32f7
    priority: 3  # 32f7
    parent:  # 32f7
    tags:  # 32f7
    - go  # 32f7
    - io_boundary  # 32f7
    - analysis_quality  # 32f7
    isbefore: []  # 32f7
    duplicate_of: []  # 32f7
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 32f7
    pr_ref:  # 32f7
    description: "FOUND 2026-09-28 while fixing INV-vusum (the typed-receiver half, which puts the receiver's TYPE in Go's module slot and prefers the exactly-named row).\n\nTHE SHAPE LEFT OVER. A method called directly on a package function's result, `pkg.Func(args).Method()`, goes through go.py's chained-call branch, which knows only the inner call's PACKAGE and sets the slot to it. So the method is still credited to a same-named package FUNCTION row by declaration order:\n    slog.New(h).Error(msg)          -> log/slog.Error          (should be log/slog.Logger.Error)\n    json.NewEncoder(w).Encode(v)    -> slot encoding/json      (the type is json.Encoder)\nMeasured on prometheus (scrape/scrape.go scrapeLoop.scrapeAndReport: `slog.New(sl.scrapeFailureLogger).Error(...)`). Every boundary is unchanged by the mislabel today (both rows of each function/method pair carry one boundary), so it is a LABEL defect, as the 17 of 18 INV-vusum pairs were.\n\nWHAT IS NOT KNOWN HERE: the return type of an external package function. _type_from_constructor_call infers `pkg.NewFoo()` -> `pkg.Foo` by the NewXxx convention, which covers json.NewEncoder but not slog.New. library_signatures/go.yaml already holds package_variables types; a return-type table for the stdlib constructors (slog.New, http.NewRequest, bufio.NewReader ...) would be the matching home.\n\nFIRST STEP: route _type_from_constructor_call's `pkg.Foo` into the chained-call branch through _external_package_for_type (the same owner the typed-local branch now builds), then measure what a small return-type table adds on alertmanager / prometheus."  # 32f7
    fields: {}  # 32f7
- op: discuss  # c655
  at: '2026-10-03T22:02:46Z'  # c655
  by: agent  # c655
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c655
  clock: 2  # c655
  nonce: c655  # c655
  message: "INTERACTION NOTE from WI-kibah's branch (jgstern-agent/fix/kibah, 4 commits, not merged; the chained-call / method-on-result code was NOT edited there).\n\n1. The call arm's resolved emit now refuses a resolver hit outside the hinted package (_go_in_hinted_package, commit 3fb8b84d20). ListNameResolver falls back to the path-sorted first of ALL candidates when a hard path hint matches none of two or more, so a hinted chained call bound an unrelated repo method: prometheus `time.Now().Add(timeout)` -> test/testutils Collector.Add before, go:time:0-0:Add:unresolved on the branch. That is the hint this item's shape propagates from the inner operand; on the branch such calls stay unresolved under the inner package's slot instead of binding a wrong repo method. Expect a merge interaction in the found branch (`if lookup_result.found:` became `if lookup_result.symbol is not None and _go_in_hinted_package(...)`), and re-measure whatever this item counts after both land.\n2. The inner-operand import test of the chained-call arm (`node_text(inner_operand) in import_aliases`) is still position-blind: a local named like an import would hand its call the import's hint. The branch adds _GoLocalScope / _bound_names(site) (commit 92379e2067); the selector arm's own import test now asks `alias not in _bound_names(node)` (commit 0adbd3fa21) and the chained arm can ask the same.\n3. The call arm's construct for resolved emits is now stamped from the syntax (bare / package-qualified: function; value receiver: method) -- relevant if this item stamps a construct on method-on-result edges."  # c655
- op: discuss  # 8a0a
